---
/* Component — PageMain
 * The page's main region — the host for a full-bleed hero above a capped row
 * holding PageMainContainer and, optionally, PageMainAside.
 *
 * One grid does both jobs. The outer tracks are the page gutters, sized with
 * the same centred-column formula PageHeader and PageFooter use for their
 * inline padding, so the content tracks between them line up with the header
 * and footer content. A hero spans full-start / full-end and bleeds edge to
 * edge; the container and aside sit between content-start and content-end.
 * PageMain itself carries no inline padding — that is what leaves the hero free
 * to bleed without margin tricks.
 *
 * The content tracks depend on whether an aside is present. Without one there
 * is a single track, so the container takes the full capped width. With one,
 * the tracks come from --bravoixr-page-aside-columns (container, gap, rail),
 * which semantics/layout.css collapses to one track below desktop so the aside
 * stacks under the container. The `:has()` test is structural — it reads this
 * component's own children, not ambient context. Astro leaves the argument
 * of :has() unscoped, so the bare `aside` matches the one PageMainAside
 * renders even though it carries PageMainAside's scope attribute, not this
 * component's. (A :global() wrapper there is emitted literally and makes the
 * whole rule invalid.)
 *
 * As the growing child of Page's flex column (flex: 1 1 auto), it absorbs the
 * leftover block space so the footer is pushed to the viewport bottom on short
 * pages. align-content: start keeps the rows at their content height while it
 * does. Inset by space-10 at the block-start and flush at the block-end, as the
 * old PageBody was; row-gap separates the hero, container and stacked aside. */
---

<main>
  <slot />
</main>

<style>
  main {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      [full-start] max(var(--bravoixr-spacing-10), calc((100% - var(--bravoixr-page-max)) / 2))
      [content-start] minmax(0, var(--bravoixr-grid-fr))
      [content-end] max(var(--bravoixr-spacing-10), calc((100% - var(--bravoixr-page-max)) / 2))
      [full-end];
    align-content: start;
    row-gap: var(--bravoixr-spacing-10);
    padding-block: var(--bravoixr-spacing-10) 0;
  }

  main:has(> aside) {
    grid-template-columns:
      [full-start] max(var(--bravoixr-spacing-10), calc((100% - var(--bravoixr-page-max)) / 2))
      [content-start] var(--bravoixr-page-aside-columns)
      [content-end] max(var(--bravoixr-spacing-10), calc((100% - var(--bravoixr-page-max)) / 2))
      [full-end];
  }
</style>
